---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import TerminalSnippet from '../../components/TerminalSnippet.astro';
import { resolvePath } from '../../utils/paths.js';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Getting Started"
  description="Install JobFoundry with Docker (default) or a ready-made AppImage / MSIX / macOS Homebrew build — then add the browser extension and start capturing jobs."
  currentPath={resolvePath('/docs/getting-started/')}
  category="Installation & Setup"
>
  <h1>Getting Started with JobFoundry</h1>
  <p>
    JobFoundry captures job listings from your browser, scores them against your
    profile using an LLM, and generates tailored ATS resumes — automatically.
    Scoring and tailoring are the core value. To unlock them you need an LLM API
    key (many providers offer a permanent free tier — see
    <a href={resolvePath('/docs/api-keys/')}>LLM API Keys</a>). Install
    JobFoundry first, then add your key in Settings.
  </p>

  <details class="collapsible-callout success">
    <summary>
      <span class="summary-inner">
        <span>✓</span>
        <span>What you need</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="chevron" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"></polyline></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <p>
        A computer (Linux, Windows 11, or macOS), a browser (Firefox, Chrome,
        Edge, or Brave), and an <strong>LLM API key</strong> — this is what
        powers scoring and tailoring. Many providers have a permanent free tier
        with no credit card required. See
        <a href={resolvePath('/docs/api-keys/')}>LLM API Keys</a> for a curated
        list. Job capture alone works without a key.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="collapsible-callout warning">
    <summary>
      <span class="summary-inner">
        <span>!</span>
        <span>Work in Progress / Beta</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="chevron" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"></polyline></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <p>
        JobFoundry is built by a solo developer scratching his own itch during a hard job search. The core flows work, but rough edges exist and active progress is happening every day. Bug reports, testing, and feedback are deeply appreciated!
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <h2>Method 1: One-line install with Docker or Podman (default &amp; recommended)</h2>
  <p>
    On Linux, macOS, or Windows (WSL2), this single command sets up everything —
    automatically detecting whether you have <code>docker compose</code>, <code>podman compose</code>,
    <code>podman-compose</code>, <code>docker-compose</code>, or compatible container tools:
  </p>
  <TerminalSnippet
    command="curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Covai-Labs/JobFoundry/main/install.sh | bash"
    title="ONE-LINE INSTALL (DOCKER / PODMAN)"
  />
  <p>
    Then open <a href="http://localhost:8080" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>http://localhost:8080</code></a>
    in your browser to see the dashboard.
  </p>

  <details class="collapsible-section">
    <summary>
      Method 2: Standalone desktop app (no containers needed)
      <svg class="chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"></polyline></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p>
        If you prefer ready-made native desktop builds without Docker or Podman, download the latest release from the
        <a href="https://github.com/Covai-Labs/JobFoundry/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Releases page</a>:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Linux:</strong> download <code>JobFoundry-&lt;version&gt;-x86_64.AppImage</code>,
          right-click → Properties → allow executing (or run
          <code>chmod +x JobFoundry-*.AppImage</code> once), then double-click to
          launch. The dashboard opens at
          <a href="http://localhost:8080" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>http://localhost:8080</code></a>.
          <em>Requires glibc 2.39+ (Fedora 40+, Ubuntu 24.04+, Debian 13+, Arch). For older distributions, use Method 1 (Docker/Podman). Convenience build — please report issues.</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Windows 11:</strong> download <code>JobFoundry-&lt;version&gt;-x64.msix</code>
          and <code>JobFoundry.cer</code>. Right-click the Start button → Terminal
          (Admin) and trust the release certificate (repeat if a release uses a new certificate), then install the package.
          <em>Convenience build — please report issues.</em>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>macOS (Apple Silicon):</strong> install via Homebrew:
          <code>brew tap covai-labs/tap &amp;&amp; brew install covai-labs/tap/jobfoundry</code>,
          then launch with <code>jobfoundry start</code>. Or download the <code>*-darwin-arm64.tar.gz</code>
          Release asset.
          <em>For Intel Macs, use Method 1 (Docker). Convenience build — please report issues.</em>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <TerminalSnippet
        command="Import-Certificate -FilePath .\JobFoundry.cer -CertStoreLocation Cert:\LocalMachine\TrustedPeople"
        title="TRUST CERTIFICATE (ADMIN POWERSHELL)"
      />
      <TerminalSnippet
        command="Add-AppxPackage -Path .\JobFoundry-<version>-x64.msix"
        title="INSTALL JOBFOUNDRY"
      />
      <p>
        Then launch <strong>JobFoundry</strong> from the Start menu. Your data and
        settings live under <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\JobFoundry\</code>, safely outside
        the app package.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details class="collapsible-section">
    <summary>
      Method 3: Manual setup (developers)
      <svg class="chevron" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"></polyline></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p>
        If you prefer to manage services yourself or contribute code:
      </p>
      <TerminalSnippet
        command="git clone https://github.com/Covai-Labs/JobFoundry.git && cd JobFoundry"
        title="CLONE REPOSITORY"
      />
      <p>
        Copy the sample configuration and add your LLM provider key:
      </p>
      <TerminalSnippet
        command="cp .env.example .env"
        title="CONFIGURE ENVIRONMENT"
      />
      <p>
        Start everything in the background:
      </p>
      <TerminalSnippet
        command="docker compose up -d"
        title="START SERVICES (DOCKER)"
      />
      <p>Or with Podman:</p>
      <TerminalSnippet
        command="podman compose up -d"
        title="START SERVICES (PODMAN)"
      />
      <p>
        For bare-metal development without containers (Node.js 26+, Python 3.12+,
        <code>uv</code>), see the <a href="https://github.com/Covai-Labs/JobFoundry/blob/main/DEVELOPMENT.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Development Guide</a>
        for per-service commands.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <h2>Next: add the browser extension</h2>
  <p>
    The extension is what captures job postings as you browse — the server
    cannot do this part (by design). Easiest: install it from your browser's
    official store:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Firefox:</strong> <a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/jobfoundry/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JobFoundry on Firefox Add-ons</a></li>
    <li><strong>Chrome / Brave:</strong> <a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/jobfoundry/kacfnebbiekbofdkgfpgmdcncgohhonm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JobFoundry on the Chrome Web Store</a></li>
    <li><strong>Edge:</strong> <a href="https://microsoftedge.microsoft.com/addons/detail/ldnjhehiegnljjlmajlipldlhdkadnpe" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">JobFoundry on Edge Add-ons</a></li>
  </ul>

  <details class="collapsible-callout">
    <summary>
      <span class="summary-inner">
        <span>◈</span>
        <span>Store listings may lag behind GitHub Releases</span>
      </span>
      <svg class="chevron" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"></polyline></svg>
    </summary>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <p>
        Store reviews take time, so the store version can trail the latest
        <a href="https://github.com/Covai-Labs/JobFoundry/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Release</a>.
        If you hit an issue, compare your installed version against the latest GitHub Release — and fall back to the
        manual <code>.zip</code> install below if you need the newest fix right away.
      </p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <p>
    Manual fallback (latest build, no building required): download the prebuilt
    <code>.zip</code> from the
    <a href="https://github.com/Covai-Labs/JobFoundry/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Releases page</a>
    and load it:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Firefox:</strong> open <code>about:debugging#/runtime/this-firefox</code>, click <strong>Load Temporary Add-on…</strong>, and select the manifest file. Note: this manual install is temporary — Firefox removes it on restart, so prefer the signed store listing above for persistent installs.</li>
    <li><strong>Chrome / Edge / Brave:</strong> open <code>chrome://extensions/</code>, enable <strong>Developer mode</strong>, click <strong>Load unpacked</strong>, and select the unzipped folder.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Then: upload your resume and browse</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the dashboard at <a href="http://localhost:8080" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>http://localhost:8080</code></a>.</li>
    <li>Go to the <strong>Resume Manager</strong> and upload your master resume (JSON Resume format).</li>
    <li>Add your LLM key in <strong>Settings</strong> (or the <code>.env</code> file for manual installs) — this is what enables scoring and tailoring. See <a href={resolvePath('/docs/api-keys/')}>LLM API Keys</a> for free options.</li>
    <li>Browse job sites normally. Listings flow into the dashboard, get scored, and appear on your Kanban board.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="next-step-box">
    <span class="next-label">NEXT STEP</span>
    <a href={resolvePath('/docs/extension/')} class="next-link">
      Install the Companion Browser Extension →
    </a>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .next-step-box {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    background-color: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-cyan);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xs);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .next-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .next-link {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent-cyan);
  }
</style>
